      "message": "I think this bit still needs expanding - this is our opportunity to define what encrypted storage is (and isn\u0027t).\n\nI suggest ending the sentence after \"VM\" and then adding further details.\n\nWe need to say at least:\n- it\u0027s encrypted using a key derived from the VM identity, not available outside the VM.\n- the encrypted data is stored in the app\u0027s private data directory. It\u0027s persistent across multiple runs of the VM, and across reboots.\n- there is no integrity or rollback protection if the encrypted data is modified.\n- it\u0027s deleted if the VM is deleted.",
